     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;background-color:#ffffff;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n<p>Hi,<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>I want to calculate differential DNA methylation of bovine fat tissues between two groups. I have two samples (cows) of each group and three replicates (three sequencing libraries) of each sample. <span style=\"font-size:12pt\">I used Bismark and\r\n got about</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> 60% unique alig</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">nment with reference genom</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">e </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">(UMD3.1</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">)\r\n of all 12 samples and CpG reports were</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> generated by Bismark Extractor. </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">I have converted CpG reports into</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> text</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> forma</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">t\r\n which was required </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">for MethylKi</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">t input.</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"> </span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Now I want your </span>guidance for reading the files in MethylKit WHERE as sampleA and sampleB are in first group. SampleC and sampleD are in second group.<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>Whether the following code will solve my purpose or guide me in this regard how to deal replicates? <br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>file.list= list ( </p>\r\n<p>&quot;sampleA_Replicate_1.txt&quot;, &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">sampleA_Replicate_2.txt</span>&quot;, &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;background-color:rgb(255,